SET ECHO OFF
STOP_ON_ERROR OFF

ECHO === JOURNAL REPLAY PROBE, PART 1 of 2 -- build the fixtures ===
ECHO
ECHO Part 1 builds four tables of KNOWN size and closes them. The harness then
ECHO hand-writes a .tbj beside each one carrying a recno that is deliberately
ECHO stale. Part 2 opens them, which is what fires
ECHO recover_table_buffer_journal (table_state.cpp:798).
ECHO
ECHO NO CRASH IS NEEDED. The reader validates the header version and the record
ECHO tags and NOTHING about the recnos, and a C marker short-circuits the group
ECHO decision lookup -- so a well-formed log with a stale recno reaches the
ECHO replay branch by the front door.

SET PATH DBF DBF/SANDBOX

ECHO
ECHO --- ARM 0, carried over from the SQL INSERT probe and never yet read ---
ECHO Does the LEGACY bare INSERT verb honour TABLE ON? NATIVE mode, so this is
ECHO cmd_sql_insert.cpp and not the SQL-mode alias.
ERASE JRN0 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 JRN0 (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE JRN0
TABLE ON
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("B0","BAREINS")
ECHO If BAREINS is listed below with no COMMIT having run, the bare verb wrote
ECHO straight to disk and is not a buffered-mode citizen.
COUNT
SMARTLIST 10
ROLLBACK
ECHO after ROLLBACK -- if BAREINS survives it was never buffered:
COUNT
SMARTLIST 10
TABLE OFF
USE

ECHO
ECHO --- JRN1: CONTROL. 2 records, journal will say I 3 -- the true next recno.
ERASE JRN1 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 JRN1 (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE JRN1
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S1","SEED1")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S2","SEED2")
COUNT
USE

ECHO
ECHO --- JRN2: STALE AND IN BOUNDS. 4 records, journal will say I 3.
ECHO Expect the else branch -> gotoRec64(3) -> record 3 overwritten.
ERASE JRN2 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 JRN2 (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE JRN2
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S1","SEED1")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S2","SEED2")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("L3","LIVE3")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("L4","LIVE4")
COUNT
USE

ECHO
ECHO --- JRN3: STALE AND OUT OF BOUNDS. 1 record, journal will say I 3.
ECHO Expect "if (recno > recCount()) continue" -> the row is DROPPED, the log
ECHO is removed anyway, and recover returns true.
ERASE JRN3 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 JRN3 (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE JRN3
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S1","SEED1")
COUNT
USE

ECHO
ECHO --- JRN4: THE PARTIAL-FIELD BLEND. 4 records, journal says I 3 setting
ECHO ONLY field 2. Expect record 3 to keep ID=L3 from the live row and take
ECHO TAG from the journal -- neither the old row nor the new one.
ERASE JRN4 CONFIRM
CREATE X64 JRN4 (ID C(4), TAG C(12))
USE JRN4
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S1","SEED1")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("S2","SEED2")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("L3","LIVE3")
INSERT (ID,TAG) VALUES ("L4","LIVE4")
COUNT
SMARTLIST 10
USE

ECHO === part 1 done -- fixtures built and closed ===
